{"id": "EUVD-2026-93197", "enisaUuid": "d746b05b-1eec-3bdc-9d1f-285b51807ca6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: abort transaction on failure to update inode for hole punching and reflinking\n\nIf we fail to update the inode we error out without aborting the\ntransaction, which can result in a persistent inconsistency if after\nthe failure the transaction is committed, as we have dropped file\nextent items from a range and either punched a hole or insert a new file\nextent item for that range (for reflinks).\n\nSo add the missing transaction abort.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2605eb9ba3bbd4c9f455cfe6b85bd28a1da7067d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/834a3b5c5f1ec0df48c1a6208f9989f4ffdaa0b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9588850bfa75c78ce73c2f6f72544d19d2e9beb6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36c68dc909845c049e0286d229bc502947239452", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97fcd34aa9fd73cefe3120ac9a82ca9d7763922f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2964-m6r5-r6cr", "CVE-2026-98269"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d7f96c5-334a-3c8c-b322-eb71558de239", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "409e57c1-5409-341a-b111-9a67c4ea5b73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "45a366bf-53aa-31a3-bfe6-26553ac8a75f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.7"}, {"id": "621c3b0e-8182-327e-b105-b0d19b899b1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2aaa66558172b017f36bf38ae69372813dedee9d <9588850bfa75c78ce73c2f6f72544d19d2e9beb6"}, {"id": "6f5f60d1-f2ab-3229-801c-07b91b8addc7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": 